# requirements-voice.in : the side environments for voice.py and qa_speech.py, per job. Versions read from PyPI on
# 2026-10-28 and 2026-11-03. NOT installed by setup.sh and NOT compiled to a hashed lock yet. Neither module installs
# from this file: each runs its job in its own uv environment with these same pins (uv run --no-project --with ...),
# so engine/requirements.txt stays Pillow and numpy only. Those pins (KokoroTs.packages in voice.py,
# qa_speech.PACKAGES) are hashed into the cache keys: change them in both places. Model and voice files are separate
# downloads (sizes and licences in references/voice.md); none is fetched without the user's yes. sapi needs nothing:
# it is part of Windows.
#
# One engine per job (VoiceStudio's engine-acceptance rule, adopted 2026-11-03): an engine is kept only while it
# holds a job nothing else does and has been run here. The sherpa-onnx Kokoro build and Piper held none and were
# never run, so they were removed in 2.3.0.

# kokoro-ts (the narrator): a side Python 3.13 environment, because kokoro-onnx 0.6.1 declares requires-python <3.14.
# Every package that changes the phonemes or the sound is pinned:
#   kokoro-onnx==0.6.1 (MIT), onnxruntime==1.31.1, phonemizer==3.4.0 (GPL-3.0),
#   espeakng-loader==0.2.4 (bundles espeak-ng, GPL-3.0), numpy==2.5.4

# qa_speech (the speech check, Q806 and Q807): a side Python 3.14 environment. Clips go in as raw float32, so
# faster-whisper never opens a file itself; av stays below 19 anyway (its file path fails with av 19,
# SYSTRAN/faster-whisper#1589, fixed on main, not in the 1.2.1 release).
faster-whisper==1.2.1
ctranslate2==4.8.5
av==18.1.0
onnxruntime==1.31.1
tokenizers==0.23.3
numpy==2.5.4
